th a modern MCP-Protocol-Version header'\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:687:        return { kind: 'legacy', reason: 'initialize', ...(requestedVersion !== undefined && { requestedVersion }) };\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:892: * - Envelope-less requests (including `initialize`) are answered with the\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:932:        case 'initialize':\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/inboundClassification.ts:935:            // initialize body's `protocolVersion` or the protocol-version\n./docs/protocol-versions.md:9:An **era** is a behavior family, not a version string. Every protocol revision from `2024-10-07` through `2025-11-25` opens with the `initialize` handshake and shares one wire behavior — the SDK calls that family `legacy`. The `2026-07-28` revision starts the `modern` era: no `initialize`, a `server/discover` advertisement instead, and a `_meta` envelope on every request.\n./docs/protocol-versions.md:33:Point the same options at a 2025-only server and `connect()` falls back to the `initialize` handshake on the same connection — one extra round trip, no error.\n./docs/protocol-versions.md:53:- Absent, or `mode: 'legacy'` — the 2025 `initialize` handshake, byte for byte. No probe.\n./docs/protocol-versions.md:54:- `mode: 'auto'` — probe with `server/discover`; fall back to `initialize` against a 2025-only server.\n./docs/protocol-versions.md:96:A probe timeout is transport-aware. On stdio a silent server is a legacy server, so `connect()` falls back to `initialize` on the same stream; on HTTP silence is an outage, so `connect()` rejects with `SdkError(RequestTimeout)` instead of misreporting a dead server as legacy. One browser exception: an opaque CORS `TypeError` during the probe falls back to the legacy era, because deployed 2025 servers commonly have allow-lists that predate the 2026 headers.\n./docs/protocol-versions.md:101:Do not default a spawn-per-invocation CLI tool to `'auto'`. On stdio, a legacy server that never answers unknown pre-`initialize` requests stalls `connect()` for the full probe timeout before falling back, and the extra round trip changes recorded transcripts. Keep the default and expose `'auto'` (or a pin) as a flag.\n./docs/protocol-versions.md:156:| Client connect                        | `initialize` handshake                                                   | `server/discover` probe (`versionNegotiation`)                     |\n./docs/protocol-versions.md:157:| Client identity on the server         | `getClientCapabilities()` / `getClientVersion()` (initialize-scoped)     | `ctx.mcpReq.envelope` (per request)                                |\n./docs/protocol-versions.md:178:- `versionNegotiation` picks the client handshake; the default is the unchanged 2025 `initialize`, no probe.\n./docs/protocol-versions.md:179:- `mode: 'auto'` probes with `server/discover` and falls back to `initialize`; a pin never falls back and rejects with `SdkError(EraNegotiationFailed)`.\n./packages/codemod/src/migrations/v1-to-v2/mappings/schemaToMethodMap.ts:2:    InitializeRequestSchema: 'initialize',\n./packages/codemod/src/migrations/v1-to-v2/mappings/schemaToMethodMap.ts:28:    InitializedNotificationSchema: 'notifications/initialized',\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/transport.ts:170:     * Sets the protocol version used for the connection (called when the initialize response is received).\n./examples/gateway/client.ts:13: *    the count is unchanged (no extra discover/initialize from the workers).\n./examples/gateway/client.ts:64:        // Adopted directly from prior — no probe, no initialize.\n./examples/gateway/client.ts:74:// each worker probed/initialized, this would read 6.\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/protocolEras.ts:4: * `initialize` handshake) and modern (2026-07-28 and later; no `initialize` —\n./packages/core-internal/src/shared/protocolEras.ts:9: * of a supported-versions