      initializer.replaceWithText(wrapped);\n./packages/codemod/src/migrations/v1-to-v2/transforms/mcpServerApi.ts:241:    if (!isZodObjectCall(initializer)) {\n./examples/shared/src/auth.ts:27:        initializeSchema(_db);\n./examples/shared/src/auth.ts:40:function initializeSchema(db: InstanceType<typeof Database>): void {\n./examples/shared/src/auth.ts:154:    console.log('[Auth] In-memory database schema initialized');\n./docs/clients/connect.md:22:`connect()` runs the `initialize` handshake and resolves once it completes. The client now holds the negotiated protocol version, the server's capabilities, and its instructions.\n./docs/clients/connect.md:101:- `new Client({ name, version })`, a transport, and `connect()` are the whole setup; `connect()` runs the `initialize` handshake.\n./test/e2e/helpers/index.ts:243:            const sid = req.headers.get('mcp-session-id') ?? undefined;\n./test/e2e/helpers/index.ts:247:                // Mirror the SDK's documented hosting pattern: an unrecognized session id is\n./test/e2e/helpers/index.ts:261:                onsessioninitialized: id => void sessions.set(id, tx),\n./test/e2e/helpers/index.ts:284:            const sid = req.headers.get('mcp-session-id') ?? undefined;\n./test/e2e/helpers/index.ts:292:                onsessioninitialized: id => void sessions.set(id, { tx, server }),\n./examples/shared/src/authServer.ts:64:        throw new Error('Auth not initialized. Call setupAuthServer first.');\n./docs/clients/middleware.md:26:Every request this transport sends now carries the header — including the requests the SDK sends that you never wrote, like `initialize`.\n./docs/clients/middleware.md:79:The `POST`s are `initialize`, the `notifications/initialized` notification, and your `tools/call`; the `GET` opens the server-to-client stream, which this server declines. Pass `statusLevel: 400` to log only failures, `includeRequestHeaders` / `includeResponseHeaders` to add headers to each line, and `logger` to replace the formatter entirely.\n./docs/clients/middleware.md:120:initialize -> HTTP 200\n./docs/clients/middleware.md:121:notifications/initialized -> HTTP 202\n./test/e2e/helpers/wire-sniffer.test.ts:16:    it('accepts a valid client initialize request', () => {\n./test/e2e/helpers/wire-sniffer.test.ts:19:                req('initialize', { protocolVersion: LATEST_PROTOCOL_VERSION, capabilities: {}, clientInfo: { name: 'c', version: '0' } }),\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:28:    'lifecycle:initialize:basic': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:32:            'Connecting sends initialize with the protocol version, client capabilities, and client info; the server responds with its own and the connection is established.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:34:    'lifecycle:initialize:instructions': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:36:        behavior: 'A server may include an instructions string in the initialize result; the client exposes it.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:38:    'lifecycle:initialized-notification': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:41:        behavior: 'After successful initialization, the client sends exactly one initialized notification, before any non-ping request.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:58:            'When the server supports the requested protocol version it echoes that version in the initialize result, and the connection proceeds at that version.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:75:            'Server-declared capabilities.experimental entries (vendor-namespaced keys, arbitrary object values) survive the initialize handshake and are exposed verbatim via client.getServerCapabilities().experimental; an undeclared key reads as undefined. Symmetric for client→server via getClientCapabilities().',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:81:            'Transport errors emitted after transport.start() but before client.connect() resolves are delivered to a client.onerror handler set prior to connect (Protocol wires transport.onerror before start() and before the initialize handshake).',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:85:    'lifecycle:initialize:server-info': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:87:        behavior: 'The initialize result identifies the server: name and version, plus title when declared.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:89:    'lifecycle:initialize:client-info': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:99:            'An initialize request carrying a protocol version the server does not support is answered with another version the server supports — the latest one — rather than an error.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:107:    'lifecycle:initialize:capabilities:minimal': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:114:            'After initialize, Server.getClientCapabilities() returns the capabilities object the client sent in InitializeRequest.params.capabilities; before initialize it returns undefined. Servers use this to gate optional features (e.g. dynamic registration) on what the connected client declared.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:121:            'After initialize, Server.getNegotiatedProtocolVersion() returns the protocol version the server responded with; before initialize it returns undefined. Matches the Client-side getter.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:142:    'protocol:cancel:initialize-not-cancellable': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:145:        behavior: 'The client never sends notifications/cancelled for the initialize request.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:149:                note: 'SDK sends notifications/cancelled for initialize when connect() is aborted; spec says initialize MUST NOT be cancelled.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:340:            'server.setRequestHandler() for a spec method that has a built-in handler (initialize, ping, logging/setLevel) replaces that handler; the user-supplied result is what the client receives. No throw on re-registration.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:809:        behavior: 'A server with a list_prompts handler advertises the prompts capability in its initialize result.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:891:        behavior: 'A server with a completion handler advertises the completions capability in its initialize result.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:930:        behavior: 'A server that emits log message notifications declares the logging capability in its initialize result.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:986:        behavior: 'A client that handles sampling requests advertises the sampling capability in its initialize request.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1443:        behavior: 'CORS configuration exposes the Mcp-Session-Id header so browser clients can read it.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1449:        behavior: 'An initialize POST without a session id creates a session and returns Mcp-Session-Id in the response headers.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1455:        behavior: 'DELETE with a valid Mcp-Session-Id terminates the session.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1459:    'hosting:session:id-charset': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1461:        behavior: 'Generated Mcp-Session-Id values contain only visible ASCII characters.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1473:        behavior: 'A non-initialize POST without Mcp-Session-Id in stateful mode returns 400.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1477:    'hosting:session:reinitialize': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1479:        behavior: 'A second initialize on an already-initialized session transport is rejected.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1485:        behavior: \"A POST carrying a valid Mcp-Session-Id routes to that session's transport with state preserved.\",\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1491:        behavior: 'A POST, GET, or DELETE with an unknown Mcp-Session-Id returns 404.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1496:                note: \"The SDK's documented hosting pattern rejects unknown session ids with 400 at the app level (see src/examples servers); the transport's own validateSession 404 is never reached, while the spec requires 404.\"\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1517:    'hosting:stateless:no-session-id': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1519:        behavior: 'In stateless mode no Mcp-Session-Id is emitted and no session validation is performed.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1798:            'createMcpExpressApp() returns an Express app with JSON body parsing and localhost host-header validation pre-applied: an MCP endpoint mounted on it serves an initialize POST over real HTTP from 127.0.0.1 and rejects a spoofed Host header with 403.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1839:                note: 'The documented per-session hosting pattern (hostPerSession) removes the transport from the session map on DELETE via onsessionclosed and answers any later request carrying the stale Mcp-Session-Id with 400 at the app level, so the spec-required 404 is never produced.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1891:    'client-transport:http:session-404-reinitialize': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1899:                note: 'On a 404 for an existing session the transport throws StreamableHTTPError (streamableHttp.ts:551) and never re-initializes — no session recovery is attempted.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1984:        behavior: 'The client can capture a resumption token, reconnect with the same session id, and receive the notifications it missed.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:1990:        behavior: 'The Mcp-Session-Id returned by initialize is stored by the client transport and sent on every subsequent request.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2448:            'When a streamable HTTP initialize fails with 400, 404, or 405, falling back to the legacy SSE client transport against the same server connects successfully.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2497:        behavior: 'After terminating a session, a fresh connection obtains a new session id and operations succeed.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2583:            \"createMcpHonoApp() hosts an McpServer over real HTTP: a StreamableHTTPClientTransport pointed at the served app completes initialize, tools/list and tools/call against a WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport mounted on the app's /mcp routes.\",\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2597:            'createMcpFastifyApp() hosts an McpServer over real HTTP: a StreamableHTTPClientTransport pointed at the listening Fastify instance completes initialize, tools/list and tools/call against a WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport wired to its /mcp routes.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2611:            'createMcpExpressApp() returns an Express app that, with a streamable HTTP server transport mounted on a POST route, serves a full initialize and tools/call exchange.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2620:        note: 'This exercises the HTTP hosting layer; the matrix transport arg is ignored, so it runs as a single streamableHttp-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs. The allowed-host control asserts initialize semantics per spec version: a 2026-era request is answered with the latest legacy version, since 2026-era revisions are never negotiated via initialize.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2628:            'createMcpHandler serves one ctx-taking factory to both protocol eras on one endpoint: with the legacy \"stateless\" slot configured, a plain client is served per request via initialize, tools/list and tools/call on the 2025 era, and an auto-negotiating client reaches 2026-07-28 via server/discover (never initialize) and gets tools/call served with the per-request _meta envelope.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2630:        note: 'Runs on the createMcpHandler entry arms (the same one-factory, legacy-stateless-slot handler shape on both): the entryStateless cell drives the 2025 leg through the slot and the entryModern cell drives the modern path, with the never-initialize/server-discover clauses asserted on the arm-recorded HTTP exchanges.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2635:            'A client pinned to the 2026-07-28 revision (versionNegotiation mode pin) connects to a strict createMcpHandler endpoint without ever sending initialize — its first request is server/discover — and an enveloped tools/call round-trips.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2638:        note: \"Runs on the entryModern arm (which hosts the entry strict via legacy: 'reject'; stateless legacy serving is the entry's own default); the body constructs the pinned client itself and asserts the never-initialize, discover-first and envelope clauses on the arm-recorded HTTP exchanges.\"\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2643:            \"A createMcpHandler endpoint configured strict (legacy: 'reject') rejects a 2025-shaped initialize with the unsupported-protocol-version error carrying the supported modern revisions in error.data.supported; nothing is silently served on the 2025 era in that mode (stateless legacy serving is the entry's default and must be turned off explicitly).\",\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2646:        note: \"Runs on the entryModern arm (which hosts the entry strict via legacy: 'reject'); the 2025-shaped initialize and the plain-client connect attempt are driven against the harness-hosted endpoint via wired.fetch/wired.url. The numeric error code is asserted by message and supported-list shape only, since it shares a code with the still-disputed header/body mismatch family.\"\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2674:            \"A real sessionful legacy wiring (per-session WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport instances keyed by Mcp-Session-Id) keeps serving the full 2025-era session lifecycle alongside a strict (legacy: 'reject') createMcpHandler endpoint via explicit user-land routing on the exported isLegacyRequest predicate: initialize issues an Mcp-Session-Id, a follow-up POST is served on that session, GET opens the standalone SSE stream, and DELETE tears the session down (a request carrying the dead session id answers 404), while envelope-claiming traffic is answered by the strict modern entry and never reaches the legacy wiring.\",\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2746:    'typescript:hosting:entry:no-session-id': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2749:            'A createMcpHandler endpoint emits no Mcp-Session-Id response header on either leg: the stateless legacy fallback hosts a sessionless server transport per request, and the modern per-request path has no session at all — every recorded exchange of a connect-then-tools/call round trip carries no session header.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2751:        note: \"Runs on the createMcpHandler entry arms; asserted on the arm-recorded httpLog response clones. The entry's BYO sessionful composition is the only way to issue a session id and is pinned by typescript:hosting:entry:byo-sessionful-legacy.\"\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2792:            'A stdio server hosted by the connection-pinned serveStdio entry serves a plain 2025 client via initialize and an auto-negotiating client on 2026-07-28 via server/discover, each on its own connection against the same factory, over a real child-process pipe.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2968:    'typescript:client-transport:http:session-id-property': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2971:            'StreamableHTTPClientTransport exposes the negotiated session id via a readable .sessionId property after initialization so consumers can persist and display it.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2975:    'typescript:client-transport:http:session-id-option': {\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2978:            'A sessionId passed to the StreamableHTTPClientTransport constructor is sent as the Mcp-Session-Id header from the first request onwards.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2999:        note: 'Against real SDK servers the relayed initialize negotiates per initialize semantics: a 2026-era request is answered with the latest legacy version, since 2026-era revisions are never negotiated via initialize.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:3006:        note: 'The test supplies its own custom Transport implementation, so the matrix transport arg is ignored; it runs as a single inMemory-labelled cell to avoid duplicate runs. On 2026-era cells the handshake is the server/discover negotiation (opted into via versionNegotiation); on 2025-era cells it is the plain initialize exchange.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:3061:            'StreamableHTTPServerTransport invokes onsessioninitialized with the new session id after initialization and onsessionclosed when the client issues DELETE, allowing hosts to maintain a session-to-transport map.',\n./examples/sse-polling/server.ts:100:// no sid + initialize → new session; unknown sid → 404; otherwise → 400).\n./examples/sse-polling/server.ts:102:    const sid = req.headers['mcp-session-id'] as string | undefined;\n./examples/sse-polling/server.ts:110:            onsessioninitialized: id => {\n./examples/sse-polling/server.ts:111:                console.error(`[${id}] Session initialized`);\n./examples/sse-polling/server.ts:119:        // Unknown/expired session ID → 404 so the client knows to re-initialize.\n./test/e2e/fixtures/dual-era-stdio-server.ts:6: * (a 2025 `initialize` handshake or 2026-07-28 per-request envelope traffic\n./packages/core-internal/src/wire/bootstrap.ts:5: * era by construction — `initialize`/`notifications/initialized` ARE the\n./packages/core-internal/src/wire/bootstrap.ts:6: * legacy handshake (`initialize` ⇒ legacy), and `server/discover` exists only\n./packages/core-internal/src/wire/bootstrap.ts:32:        case 'initialize':\n./packages/core-internal/src/wire/bootstrap.ts:33:        case 'notifications/initialized': {\n./examples/elicitation/server.ts:5: * connection (`--legacy`, the `initialize` handshake) the server uses the\n./examples/elicitation/server.ts:17: * `elicitation/create` needs the `initialize`-declared client capabilities and\n./examples/elicitation/server.ts:257:        const sid = req.headers['mcp-session-id'] as string | undefined;\n./examples/elicitation/server.ts:263:                onsessioninitialized: id => {\n./examples/cli-client/README.md:120:--legacy                use the 2025 initialize handshake instead of probing for 2026-07-28\n./packages/client/CHANGELOG.md:49:  connect time and conservatively falls back to the plain legacy `initialize` handshake on the same connection unless the outcome is definitive modern evidence (with a supported-versions list that has no 2025-era entry there is nothing to fall back to, and connect rejects\n./packages/client/CHANGELOG.md:51:  a legacy server and falls back to `initialize` on the same stream, on HTTP it rejects with a typed timeout error.\n./packages/client/CHANGELOG.md:109:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - SEP-2243 `Mcp-Param-*` client-side mirroring (protocol revision 2026-07-28). On a 2026-07-28 connection over Streamable HTTP, `Client.callTool()` now mirrors tool arguments designated with `x-mcp-header` in the tool's `inputSchema` into `Mcp-Param-{Name}` HTTP headers (with the spec's `=?base64?…?=` sentinel encoding for values that are not safe plain-ASCII field values), and on a non-stdio modern connection `Client.listTools()` (and the client's internal `tools/list` cache) exclude tool definitions whose `x-mcp-header` declarations violate the spec's constraints, logging a warning naming the tool and the reason. The legacy-era `callTool` and `listTools` paths are unchanged at the wire level. Browser environments skip mirroring (dynamically named headers cannot be statically allow-listed for credentialed CORS); a conforming SEP-2243 server will reject a `tools/call` whose body carries a non-null value for an `x-mcp-header` parameter when the matching header is absent, so calling such a tool with that argument from a browser is a known limitation. New `CallToolRequestOptions.toolDefinition` lets callers supply the tool definition directly so mirroring and output-schema validation can run without a prior `tools/list`. `TransportSendOptions.headers` is added (additive, optional) for per-request HTTP headers; the Streamable HTTP transport skips reserved standard/auth header names (`authorization`, `mcp-protocol-version`, `mcp-method`, `mcp-name`, `mcp-session-id`, `content-type`); transports that share a single channel (stdio, in-memory) ignore it.\n./packages/client/CHANGELOG.md:125:  listChanged/subscribe-class capabilities until the `subscriptions/listen` flow ships; servers with today's default list are unchanged and keep answering `-32601`. The `initialize` handshake is now era-aware in the other direction: its accept check and counter-offer consult\n./packages/client/CHANGELOG.md:126:  only the legacy subset of the supported versions — a 2026-era revision is never negotiated via `initialize` — so a 2025-era client can never be offered a 2026 version string; with the default list this is byte-identical to previous behavior. Serving the 2026 revision to\n./packages/core-internal/src/wire/rev2026-07-28/registry.ts:5: * `initialize`, `notifications/initialized`, `ping`, `logging/setLevel`,\n./test/integration/test/client/client.test.ts:17:test('should initialize with matching protocol version', async () => {\n./test/integration/test/client/client.test.ts:22:            if (message.method === 'initialize') {\n./test/integration/test/client/client.test.ts:55:    // Should have sent initialize with latest version\n./test/integration/test/client/client.test.ts:58:            method: 'initialize',\n./test/integration/test/client/client.test.ts:75:test('should initialize with supported older protocol version', async () => {\n./test/integration/test/client/client.test.ts:81:            if (message.method === 'initialize') {\n./test/integration/test/client/client.test.ts:133:            if (message.method === 'initialize') {\n./test/integration/test/client/client.test.ts:164:        sessionId: 'existing-session-id'\n./test/integration/test/client/client.test.ts:169:    // No initialize request should have been sent (sess